(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// sys.monitoring's call-family events (PEP 669; queue 220, Python/instrumentation.c and Python/legacy_tracing.c of"] [4 1 "// CPython 3.14.10, PSF License Agreement): the tools' registry (use_tool_id, free_tool_id, clear_tool_id, get_tool),"] [5 1 "// their global events (set_events, get_events) and callbacks (register_callback), and the events a profiler needs:"] [6 1 "// PY_START, PY_RESUME, PY_THROW, PY_RETURN, PY_YIELD, PY_UNWIND at a frame's start and end (runFrames), CALL, C_RETURN"] [7 1 "// and C_RAISE at the call sites of the loop and of compiled code (eval.go, aot.go). sys.setprofile is the legacy tool"] [8 1 "// over them (PY_MONITORING_SYS_PROFILE_ID 6), as legacy_tracing.c makes it. _lsprof (builtins_lsprof.go) is a tool."] [9 1 "//"] [10 1 "// Off, an event costs one load of monEvents (0 when no tool has an event) and a branch. A callback runs with the thread's"] [11 1 "// tracing count up (tstate->tracing): no event fires inside it. Since queue 281 the local events (set_local_events, per"] [12 1 "// code object), LINE, INSTRUCTION, JUMP and BRANCH_LEFT/RIGHT from the loop (trace.go's traceInstr, the offsets the"] [13 1 "// bytecode view's), RAISE, RERAISE, EXCEPTION_HANDLED and STOP_ITERATION fire too. Since queue 274b a callback's DISABLE turns its event off at the"] [14 1 "// location for the tool (the code object and the offset; an event that cannot be disabled raises ValueError and loses"] [15 1 "// its callback), restart_events turns them on again, C_RETURN and C_RAISE follow CALL as CPython's ancillary events,"] [16 1 "// and sys.monitoring's C API (PyMonitoring_EnterScope, the _PyMonitoring_Fire*Event functions) is pyctypes' over"] [17 1 "// MonitoringTools and MonitoringCall below."] [18 1 "// CALL's instruction_offset is 2 x the IR's instruction (f_lasti's unit)."] [20 1 "// the events' numbers (the bit index of sys.monitoring.events' values)"] [32 2 "// monNLocal are the local events (_PY_MONITORING_LOCAL_EVENTS: PY_START to STOP_ITERATION)"] [34 2 "// monProfileTool is the legacy profiler's tool (PY_MONITORING_SYS_PROFILE_ID)"] [39 1 "// monCallFamily are the events a profiler uses (legacy_tracing.c's for sys.setprofile)"] [43 1 "// monTool is a tool's registration: its name (nil: free), its global events, its callbacks by event."] [48 2 "// native, for the legacy profiler: called in place of cb"] [54 2 "// monEvents is the union of every tool's global events: the hooks' one load"] [56 2 "// monMissing and monDisable are sys.monitoring.MISSING and DISABLE"] [59 2 "// monTracing are the threads running a callback (tstate->tracing); under the GIL"] [61 2 "// monVersion is the interpreter's instrumentation version (queue 274b, the C API's PyMonitoring_EnterScope): raised"] [62 2 "// when a tool's global events change (monSeen: the events at the last change), as _PyMonitoring_SetEvents does"] [65 2 "// monOthers is the union of the events of the tools but the legacy tracer, the local ones included (queue 281):"] [66 2 "// traceInstr's events for the tools"] [68 2 "// monToolVersion is each tool's version (interp->monitoring_tool_versions): clear_tool_id raises it, which turns"] [69 2 "// off the code objects' local events set before (queue 281)"] [71 2 "// monLocalCodes are the code objects with local events (set_local_events), whose union monEvents holds"] [75 1 "// monLocalEvents are a code object's local events by tool (_co_monitoring->local_monitors, queue 281), each with the"] [76 1 "// tool's version when set: an older version's events are kept (get_local_events reads them, as CPython's) but fire no more."] [82 1 "// monLocal is tool i's live local events of c."] [90 1 "// monWants is whether tool i has event bit for code c: its global events, or c's local ones."] [98 1 "// monUpdate recomputes monEvents, and breakMonitor in the eval breaker: a frame's start checks the breaker alone, so"] [99 1 "// its PY_START costs nothing while no tool has an event."] [127 1 "// monEventBit is the bit of a tool's events that has it fire ev: CALL's for C_RETURN and C_RAISE, the ancillary"] [128 1 "// events (CPython's tools for them are CALL's)."] [136 1 "// monFire calls the tools' callbacks of event ev with args; the first error is returned (raised where the event is)."] [142 1 "// monFireAt is monFire with the event's location (DISABLE's) at off: the tools whose global events or f's code's local"] [143 1 "// events have ev, the most significant first (call_instrumentation_vector's order, queue 281)."] [151 15 "// no event inside the code that stands for C (trace.go's inCImpl)"] [175 3 "// the event the callback runs for (tstate->what_event: f_lineno's setter reads it; queue 281)"] [192 4 "// call_instrumentation_vector (queue 274b): DISABLE turns the event off at this location for the tool until"] [193 4 "// restart_events; the other events cannot be disabled, their callback is removed"] [207 1 "// monUndisable drops tool's disabled locations of the events it no longer has (of code c's only, c not nil): an event"] [208 1 "// turned off and on again is instrumented anew, DISABLE's removal gone (queue 281)."] [217 1 "// monSite is an instrumented location: a code object, an event and its offset (DISABLE's unit)."] [224 1 "// monDisabled are the locations DISABLE turned off, by tool (restart_events clears them)."] [227 1 "// monSiteOf is ev's location in f (its offset the callback's second argument), and whether ev is a local"] [228 1 "// (instrumented) event DISABLE can turn off (PY_MONITORING_IS_INSTRUMENTED_EVENT: the events below RAISE)."] [246 1 "// monEnter is a frame's start in runFrames: PY_THROW for an exception thrown into a generator's frame, PY_START for a"] [247 1 "// frame at its first instruction, else PY_RESUME."] [266 1 "// monLeave is a frame's return of v in runFrames: PY_YIELD when it is suspended, else PY_RETURN."] [278 1 "// monUnwind is a frame left by exc (PY_UNWIND); a callback's error replaces the exception."] [291 1 "// monCall is CALL before a call of callable from f, arg0 its first argument (self for a method) or nil."] [303 1 "// monCallee is a CALL's callable and first argument as CPython's instrumented CALL has them (queue 281): a bound method"] [304 1 "// expanded into its function and self (_MAYBE_EXPAND_METHOD), a built-in method bound to its object with that object"] [305 1 "// (the method form's LOAD_ATTR: the descriptor and self; pyi's IR binds it at the attribute load)."] [315 28 "// a slot wrapper bound by the method form's LOAD_ATTR (int().__repr__())"] [326 1 "// monExpandMethod is CALL's _MAYBE_EXPAND_METHOD for its events (queue 293): a method object over a built-in function"] [327 1 "// (classmethod(repr)'s) gives CALL and C_RETURN the function, self their first argument, so the profiler's c_call and"] [328 1 "// c_return name the function (test_sys_setprofile's test_method_with_c_function, gh-122029). CALL_FUNCTION_EX does not"] [329 1 "// expand: its events name the method object, and the profiler gives no c_call."] [339 1 "// monCReturn is C_RETURN or C_RAISE after a call of callable, not a Python function, from f: the call's result, or a"] [340 1 "// callback's error."] [359 1 "// monCallC is a call of a callable that is not a Python function from f with monitoring on: CALL, the call, then"] [360 1 "// C_RETURN or C_RAISE."] [373 1 "// isPyFunction is whether a call of o runs a Python frame (a function, or a bound method of one): no C events."] [386 1 "// the legacy profiler (sys.setprofile): each thread's function, and how many threads have one"] [401 1 "// setProfile is _PyEval_SetProfile for t: fn None removes it."] [411 19 "// as setTrace's"] [415 1 "// profileCFunc is the C function a CALL's callable stands for (legacy_tracing.c's sys_profile_call_or_return): a"] [416 1 "// built-in function or method itself, a method descriptor bound to its first argument; nil for any other callable."] [430 1 "// builtinOwner is the type in arg0's type's MRO whose dict holds b (a method descriptor's d_type), or nil."] [443 1 "// profileEvent is the legacy tool's callback: the thread's profile function called as (frame, event, arg); an error"] [444 1 "// removes it (sys.setprofile(None)) and is raised."] [478 1 "// newMonitoringModule is sys.monitoring."] [536 3 "// _PyMonitoring_ClearToolId: the callbacks, the global events, and (the tool's version raised) its local events"] [596 3 "// monitoring_set_events_impl (queue 274b): C_RETURN and C_RAISE are not kept, they follow CALL (call_one_instrument's"] [597 3 "// tools for them are CALL's); BRANCH is BRANCH_LEFT and BRANCH_RIGHT"] [630 4 "// BRANCH (queue 281: _PyMonitoring_RegisterCallback's legacy branch handlers): the callback for BRANCH_LEFT and"] [631 4 "// BRANCH_RIGHT, each wrapped so that its DISABLE turns off the other side too; the old BRANCH_LEFT's returned"] [656 2 "// the local events (queue 281; monitoring_get_local_events_impl, monitoring_set_local_events_impl,"] [657 2 "// _PyMonitoring_SetLocalEvents)"] [730 3 "// _PyMonitoring_RestartEvents (queue 274b): every disabled location on again"] [736 3 "// monitoring__all_events_impl (queue 281): each ungrouped event's tools with it among their global events"] [748 1 "// monCallSite is a call site's monitoring (queue 220): CALL fired; a callable that is no Python function called here"] [749 1 "// with C_RETURN or C_RAISE after it (done true, its result); a Python function's call left to the site (done false)."] [756 14 "// CALL's, not CALL_FUNCTION_EX's (monExpandMethod)"] [770 1 "// callStackMon is callStack's monitoring: monCallSite over the call's callable and arguments on f's stack, which a C"] [771 1 "// callable's call pops."] [797 1 "// The C API's view of the monitors (queue 274b; Python/instrumentation.c's PyMonitoring_EnterScope and"] [798 1 "// capi_call_instrumentation, CPython 3.14.10): the C half is pyctypes' (capi_monitoring.go)."] [800 1 "// monEventNames are instrumentation.c's event_names, by event number."] [805 1 "// MonitoringVersion is the instrumentation version PyMonitoring_EnterScope compares with a scope's."] [808 1 "// MonitoringTools is _Py_GlobalMonitors' tools[ev]: the tools whose global events have ev. An extension's tool's events"] [809 1 "// as set_events stores them (monitoring_set_events_impl: BRANCH as BRANCH_LEFT and BRANCH_RIGHT, C_RETURN and C_RAISE"] [810 1 "// left out, they follow CALL)."] [828 1 "// MonitoringEventName is event_names[ev]."] [836 1 "// MonitoringCall is call_one_instrument for the C API: tool's callback of ev called with args (0: none, or it returned;"] [837 1 "// 1: it returned DISABLE), with the thread's tracing count up. A native tool (the legacy profiler) has no callback for"] [838 1 "// an extension's events."] [862 1 "// MonitoringClearCallback clears tool's callback of ev (capi_call_instrumentation's \"Callback removed\")."] [869 1 "// monBranchHandlers are the legacy branch handlers' callbacks, by handler (register_callback's BRANCH; queue 281)."] [872 1 "// monBranchHandler is branch_handler_vectorcall: tool's callback cb for one side of BRANCH; its DISABLE also turns off"] [873 1 "// the other side at the source (a FOR_ITER's left only from its right, as CPython cannot find the POP_ITER)."] [877 3 "// \"Already disabled\": the source instruction no longer instrumented for the tool (a FOR_ITER whose left was"] [878 3 "// disabled, a jump whose right was) has its other side disabled too"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[84 20] [156 24] [156 32] [162 41] [180 21] [235 29] [283 79] [284 29] [307 33] [313 32] [314 36] [319 47] [331 32] [332 32] [353 78] [366 40] [375 27] [379 36] [423 36] [437 25] [469 20] [526 29] [566 28] [583 22] [593 49] [617 13] [617 29] [638 38] [648 37] [703 22] [738 13] [738 31] [739 34] [759 44] [780 44] [850 20] [879 37] [880 30] [883 31] [914 30]]} (go/file "monitoring.go" :imports [])

;; sys.monitoring's call-family events (PEP 669; queue 220, Python/instrumentation.c and Python/legacy_tracing.c of
;; CPython 3.14.10, PSF License Agreement): the tools' registry (use_tool_id, free_tool_id, clear_tool_id, get_tool),
;; their global events (set_events, get_events) and callbacks (register_callback), and the events a profiler needs:
;; PY_START, PY_RESUME, PY_THROW, PY_RETURN, PY_YIELD, PY_UNWIND at a frame's start and end (runFrames), CALL, C_RETURN
;; and C_RAISE at the call sites of the loop and of compiled code (eval.go, aot.go). sys.setprofile is the legacy tool
;; over them (PY_MONITORING_SYS_PROFILE_ID 6), as legacy_tracing.c makes it. _lsprof (builtins_lsprof.go) is a tool.
;;
;; Off, an event costs one load of monEvents (0 when no tool has an event) and a branch. A callback runs with the thread's
;; tracing count up (tstate->tracing): no event fires inside it. Since queue 281 the local events (set_local_events, per
;; code object), LINE, INSTRUCTION, JUMP and BRANCH_LEFT/RIGHT from the loop (trace.go's traceInstr, the offsets the
;; bytecode view's), RAISE, RERAISE, EXCEPTION_HANDLED and STOP_ITERATION fire too. Since queue 274b a callback's DISABLE turns its event off at the
;; location for the tool (the code object and the offset; an event that cannot be disabled raises ValueError and loses
;; its callback), restart_events turns them on again, C_RETURN and C_RAISE follow CALL as CPython's ancillary events,
;; and sys.monitoring's C API (PyMonitoring_EnterScope, the _PyMonitoring_Fire*Event functions) is pyctypes' over
;; MonitoringTools and MonitoringCall below.
;; CALL's instruction_offset is 2 x the IR's instruction (f_lasti's unit).


